The current implementation homes record/play to the normalized upper-left through `uinput`; it neither queries X11 nor targets `(960, 540)`. I’ll replace that command-level initialization with an X11 cursor calibrator that queries the current pointer, validates screen geometry, warps to the exact pixel, and verifies the result; recorded movement will remain an ordered edge path so replay preserves every measured delta rather than smoothing away turns.
